 "notes": "NIST AM test artifact, page 1 of the 2-page EngineeringDrawing.pdf (raster images in a PDF — treated as 'scan'). Page 1 is views only: no title block, no notes, no material, no general tolerance — those groups are complete with no rows. Every geometric tolerance VALUE is the placeholder 'xx' (by design in the source), so GD&T rows match on characteristic and datums only (no tolerance key); frames without datums have no partial. Frames (23): straightness 'xx' ×7 (one with each of datums F, G, D, E and H as their datum feature carriers, and the second row under the parallelism-H and perpendicularity-H composite frames); parallelism 'xx' to F, G, D, E and H; perpendicularity 'xx' H; cylindricity 'xx' on the centre boss; concentricity 'xx' B ×2, each stacked over a circularity 'xx' (so circularity ×2); position 'xx' B C ×5 in SECTION B-B on the basic 60 / 50 / 40 / 30 / 20. Datum feature symbols A–H, one each. Symbolic hole callouts 'Ød1 THRU x4' and 'Ød2 x16' carry NO numeric size and are not recorded. Section labels (A-A … D-D), view arrows and section letters are not recorded. Dimensions (34, complete; all grey reference-style text): SECTION A-A 3, 6, 3, 6, 60.00° ×2, 'Ø3 ↧3', 'Ø6 ↧5' (diameter + depth rows); SECTION B-B basic 60, 50, 40, 30, 20 (boxed) and 7, 10; SECTION C-C 2.50, 25, 2.50, 1, 1; SECTION D-D 2, 1.50, 1, 0.50, 0.25 (left), 2, 1.50, 1, 0.50, 0.25 (right), 2, 2 (heights). Units are not stated on the page. Notes group not complete."
